# Buyable Antonio Stradivari (Stradivarius) violins — web research snapshot

**Generated:** 2026-05-17 (UTC)  
**Method:** Targeted public-web search and retrieval of listed sources. This is **not** an exhaustive crawl of the entire internet; authentic Strads are almost never sold through mass-market storefronts, and availability changes daily. Verify status, provenance, and price with the seller before any transaction.

---

## A. Instruments with a documented, public “for sale / request information” path (check current status)

### 1. The 1731 ‘Heifetz, Piel’ Stradivari (Antonio Stradivari, c. 1731)

- **Channel:** Tarisio Private Sales (inquiry / private treaty).  
- **Public page:** https://tarisio.com/heifetz/  
- **Summary:** Marketed as coming to market after decades in private hands; page invites “Request Information” and references sale through Tarisio Private Sales.  
- **Press / context:** https://www.thestrad.com/news/heifetzs-1731-stradivari-to-be-sold-by-tarisio/19511.article  
- **Contact (as cited in press):** heifetz@tarisio.com (confirm on Tarisio’s official site).  
- **Note:** As of page fetch in this research cycle, wording still referred to an upcoming spring sale; **confirm with Tarisio** whether the instrument remains available or has transacted.

