## B. Recently completed public sales (no longer buyable at the original listing; useful for provenance and price context)

### 2. The 1714 ‘Joachim-Ma’ Stradivari

- **Was offered:** Sotheby’s New York, February 2025.  
- **Reported result:** approximately **USD 11.25–11.3 million** (hammer ~USD 10 million; figures vary slightly by source).  
- **Lot / catalog (archived listing):** https://www.sothebys.com/buy/ce9ed3bd-5031-43ec-bf46-a0af012b949b/lots/e2c3308d-a2a2-4625-98d6-aecba2711ae2  
- **Sotheby’s article:** https://www.sothebys.com/en/articles/joachim-ma-stradivarius-achieves-11-3m-at-sothebys  

### 3. The c. 1737 ‘McKay’ Stradivari (Kodner, “The McKay”)

- **Auction:** Kodner Galleries, 8 October 2025.  
- **Reported result:** **USD 2.75 million** (including buyer’s premium), per trade press summarizing the sale.  
- **Original auction lot page (archive):** https://www.kodner.com/auctions/2025/10/08/stradivarius-violin-estate-jewelry-decoration/81  
- **Third-party auction mirror:** https://www.bidsquare.com/online-auctions/kodner/antonio-stradivari-cremona-c1737-violin-8195024  

### 4. The ‘Salabue, Matsuda’ Stradivari (early Stradivari; unique remade front c. 1716)

- **Auction:** Tarisio, New York, 14 November 2024.  
- **Reported result:** **USD 3.48 million** (including buyer’s premium).  
- **Sale page (may show closed auction):** https://tarisio.com/salabue/  
- **Press:** https://www.thestrad.com/news/salabue-matsuda-stradivari-violin-fetches-348-million-at-auction/18917.article  

