## C. Specialist venues that regularly broker authentic Stradivari sales (inventory not always public; buyable through relationship / private treaty / auction)

| Venue | Role | Starting point |
|--------|------|----------------|
| **Tarisio** | Auctions + private sales for fine instruments | https://tarisio.com/ |
| **Ingles & Hayday** | Auctions, London shop, private sales | https://ingleshayday.com/ — notable sales index e.g. https://ingleshayday.com/makers/stradivari-antonio/ |
| **J & A Beare** | Major dealer; acquisition / buying desk | https://www.beares.com/buying/ |
| **Sotheby’s / Christie’s / Bonhams** | Periodic single-owner or curated sales | Search each house’s site for “Antonio Stradivari” or “Stradivari violin”. Example past lot: https://www.christies.com/lot/lot-4705238 (Hammer — historical). |
| **Amati** | Specialist dealer / maker pages (market context) | https://amati.com/maker/stradivari-antonio/ |

**Upcoming auction calendar (verify catalogs for actual Stradivari lots):** Tarisio and other houses sometimes publish Berlin / London / New York dates (e.g. Berlin May 2026 mentioned in secondary summaries); **only lots in the published catalog** count as confirmed offerings.

---

## D. Mass-market “Stradivarius” listings (violins / copies — usually **not** Antonio Stradivari)

Thousands of inexpensive instruments bear the **Stradivarius model name** or facsimile labels. Those are **not** the Cremonese master’s work. If the goal is an **authentic** Antonio Stradivari violin, assume multimillion-dollar pricing, full certification (W.E. Hill & Sons, Beare, Tarisio, etc.), and sale through the channels above—not general e-commerce “add to cart” listings.

---

## E. How to extend this file

1. Check Tarisio, Ingles & Hayday, and major auction house **current** catalogs.  
2. Search news from **The Strad**, **The Violin Channel**, and dealer press releases for “Stradivari” + “sale” or “auction”.  
3. For any offered instrument, collect: maker attribution, date/nickname, certificates, estimate or ask, sale venue, lot URL, and sale date/result.

---

*End of snapshot.*
